# ICT-FaceKit generic neutral head, trimmed for the Face API avatar.
#
# Source:  https://github.com/USC-ICT/ICT-FaceKit  FaceXModel/generic_neutral_mesh.obj
# Commit:  aa8c24174d00f370ce3f7d99e56ff3c734037805  (2020-07-23)
# Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 USC Institute for Creative Technologies
#          The full licence is in LICENSE.txt next to this file.
#
# Vertex numbering is unchanged from upstream, so the 68 Multi-PIE landmark indices the
# ICT-FaceKit README documents still address the vertices they name. Removed here: the
# texture coordinates, and the faces of the parts the avatar never shows - teeth, gums and
# tongue, lacrimal fluid, the eye blend and occlusion shells, the eyelashes, and the neck
# below a line a little under the chin, which upstream flares into a collar wider than the
# head. Their vertices are still present, and unreferenced, which keeps the numbering intact.
#
# Groups below name the parts, so a reader can tell what is what and the loader can give the
# mouth socket and the eyes their own materials.

